@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+---
+id: task-004-hourly-rental-pricing
+type: task
+title: "Hourly rental pricing"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Hourly rental pricing
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and today the desk has to turn them away. Customers should be
+able to rent by the hour.
+
+## Requested behaviour
+
+`addEquipment` also accepts `hourlyPrice`: the price of one hour of rental, in euro cents. A rental shorter than a
+day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the item's `hourlyPrice` for each hour. An item without an
+hourly price cannot be rented by the hour.
+
+## Interpretation
+
+- `hourlyPrice` is optional. When given, it must be a positive integer number of euro cents, as `dailyPrice` is.
+- An hourly rental is a period that starts and ends on a whole hour in UTC (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:00:00Z`) and lasts less
+  than 24 hours. It may cross midnight, e.g. 22:00 to 02:00 is 4 hours.
+- The total is `hourlyPrice` times the number of hours. No long-stay discount applies: an hourly rental is always
+  under a day.
+- A period of exactly 24 hours, or longer, must still start and end at midnight UTC, as before. Times that are not on
+  the hour (e.g. 10:30) are still rejected.
+- A midnight-to-midnight period (`YYYY-MM-DD` or `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00Z`) is a daily rental, priced as before.
+- An item without `hourlyPrice` asked for an hourly rental throws. Its daily rentals are unchanged.
+- Hourly periods share the same booking rules: an hourly booking blocks overlapping periods of the same item, and
+  `availability` lists the item for a period only when it is free for the whole period.
+- `quote` and `book` return the hourly total in `total`, as they do for daily rentals.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice` and rejects an invalid one.
+- A 3-hour rental of an item with `hourlyPrice` 1 000 is quoted and booked at 3 000.
+- A rental crossing midnight (22:00 to 02:00) is priced by its hours.
+- A rental of an item without `hourlyPrice` by the hour throws; its daily rentals still work.
+- A 24-hour period not starting at midnight, and times that are not on the hour, still throw.
+- Hourly bookings block overlapping periods, and `availability` respects them.
+- Tests are deterministic and in-process, with no external services.
+- The README describes hourly rental and `hourlyPrice`.
